# Example .semgrepignore for the static analysis Gate. Copy it to the
# repository root as .semgrepignore only if you need it.
#
# A .semgrepignore replaces Opengrep's default ignore list, which skips paths
# such as test/, tests/, vendor/, build/, dist/ and node_modules/. Once the
# file exists, those paths are scanned unless you list them here, and every
# entry, including a copied default, is a Suppression that needs a reason and
# an expiry.
#
# Entries use .gitignore syntax. The comment directly above an entry gives its
# reason and expiry, and covers the consecutive entries below it, up to a
# blank line. The Gate fails when an entry has no reason, no expiry, a date
# that isn't YYYY-MM-DD, or a past expiry, and warns 14 days ahead.

# reason: vendored third-party library, patched upstream only expires: 2027-03-31
vendor/

# reason: test fixtures build deliberately unsafe inputs expires: 2027-03-31
tests/fixtures/
test/fixtures/
